{"kind":"request","text":"Review J2: a reviewer reads a diff, an interdiff and a file at exact commits in a Change card. Note: notes/implementation/2026-11-01-j2-views.md. Gate passed at e143d731; this head adds only the note and its manifest on top.\n\nThe J2 acceptance has not happened, and landing this head does not meet it. No deployed Worker, real room, Artifacts repository or desktop AI app ran this code. The reviewer's path ran as a composed local proxy, which the note labels part by part.\n\nHosted MCP: open nothing. Opening the endpoint or naming `diff` does not reach these views, because packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts passes no views and no Git reader. So this request names no Worker to open and no tool to add. The views run in the local stdio process apps/views/src/node.ts against dap-demo. If the views must reach a person by a hosted URL alone, hosted.ts needs a view source and a Git reader. I did not build that, and the planner decides it.\n\nWhat a person must do, and what the planner must name: the note holds the witness script. The planner names a room on dap-demo with a real repository and the J4 change definition active, because `propose-file` names no commit. The person adds one entry to the desktop AI app's MCP configuration and presses the reads. J4's remaining phases gate version 1 and version 2 through hold@2. The run must show three things no run has shown: whether the app renders the card from this stdio process, whether Artifacts upload-pack gives a read token an unadvertised commit under refs/artroom/staged/, and whether the app takes a view_act answer of about 90 KiB.\n\nPlease read closely:\n1. The rebase design, in \"How an interdiff handles a rebased version 2\". The manifest's `base` decides. Each changed path falls in one of four groups, and a path the four commits cannot separate shows both patches and assigns no line. I read the request's \"the reviewer's change\" as the change under review, and the note says so.\n2. The trust in `base